From: Runeon Contributors <dev@runeon.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wined3d: Clear the active lights when cleaning up a stateblock state.

wined3d_stateblock_state_cleanup() frees every light in the light tree
but leaves light_state->lights[], the array of enabled lights, pointing
at them. state_cleanup() clears that array first; the stateblock path
does not.

For a stateblock that is destroyed this does not matter, but
wined3d_stateblock_reset() keeps the light state: it clears
stateblock_state, points it back at the same wined3d_light_state and
only re-initialises the tree. The array keeps the freed pointers. d3d8
and d3d9 reset their device state this way on IDirect3DDevice*::Reset(),
after which wined3d_device_apply_stateblock() reads the freed lights
when it updates the FFP light constants, and
wined3d_light_state_enable_light() treats the stale slots as taken. A
D3D8 application resetting its device then logged "Unhandled light type"
with garbage values thousands of times.

Clear the array before freeing the lights, as state_cleanup() does.

diff --git a/dlls/wined3d/stateblock.c b/dlls/wined3d/stateblock.c
--- a/dlls/wined3d/stateblock.c
+++ b/dlls/wined3d/stateblock.c
@@ -646,6 +646,11 @@ static void wined3d_stateblock_state_cleanup(struct wined3d_stateblock_state *st
         }
     }
 
+    /* wined3d_stateblock_reset() keeps the light state, so the active light
+     * array must not keep pointing at the lights freed below. */
+    for (i = 0; i < WINED3D_MAX_ACTIVE_LIGHTS; ++i)
+        state->light_state->lights[i] = NULL;
+
     RB_FOR_EACH_ENTRY_DESTRUCTOR(light, cursor, &state->light_state->lights_tree, struct wined3d_light_info, entry)
     {
         if (light->changed)
